WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.028
Local large-language-model infrastructure is the hardware, runtime software, storage,

00:00:04.028 --> 00:00:04.901
interfaces, controls,

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:10.138
and operating practices used to run model inference on systems you control.

00:00:10.138 --> 00:00:15.812
The model may live on a laptop, workstation, gaming PC, mini PC, server,

00:00:15.812 --> 00:00:17.557
or managed private environment.

00:00:17.557 --> 00:00:22.358
Local inference sends prompts to a model running in that environment.

00:00:22.358 --> 00:00:28.468
A cloud API sends requests to an external provider under its service, security, pricing,

00:00:28.468 --> 00:00:29.777
and data-handling model.

00:00:29.777 --> 00:00:34.578
Hybrid designs may route different workloads according to sensitivity, quality, cost,

00:00:34.578 --> 00:00:35.451
or availability.

00:00:35.451 --> 00:00:40.688
Hardware choices include CPUs, discrete GPUs, unified-memory systems such as Apple Silicon,

00:00:40.688 --> 00:00:43.743
system memory, storage, networking, power, and cooling.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:48.544
Software choices include model formats, runtimes, drivers, user interfaces, local APIs,

00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:50.290
monitoring, and access control.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:54.654
Local operation can improve data control, offline capability, experimentation, customization,

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.273
and cost predictability for steady workloads.

00:00:57.273 --> 00:01:02.073
It also transfers responsibility for hardware limits, software updates, security, backups,

00:01:02.073 --> 00:01:05.128
availability, and model governance to the operator.

00:01:05.128 --> 00:01:07.747
Performance depends on the complete configuration.

00:01:07.747 --> 00:01:12.548
Model architecture, parameter count, quantization, context length, prompt size, batch behavior,

00:01:12.548 --> 00:01:18.658
concurrency, runtime, acceleration backend, and cooling can matter as much as the device name.

00:01:18.658 --> 00:01:23.022
The right question is not whether local is always better.

00:01:23.022 --> 00:01:29.132
It is whether a measured local system meets the task's quality, privacy, latency, throughput,

00:01:29.132 --> 00:01:33.060
cost, and operational requirements more effectively than available alternatives.
